  "system": {
    "slug": "fenris-mech",
    "details": {
      "level": {
        "value": 1
      },
      "publicNotes": "<p>The FENRIS is Cerberus' quadruped assault drone: a cheap, fast, four-legged chassis built around one idea, which is closing the distance before anyone can bring a gun to bear. Deployed from drop crates in packs, they sprint at the nearest heat signature, leap, and drive electrified claws into whatever they land on. Anything left of the frame discharges its power cell on destruction, so putting one down at arm's length is nearly as dangerous as letting it reach you.</p><p><strong>Pack Deployment:</strong> FENRIS mechs are almost never encountered alone. A crate releases four to six at once.</p><p><strong>Overload Vulnerability:</strong> Exposed power couplings give the chassis weakness 3 to electricity — a single Overload will usually cripple one.</p>",
      "privateNotes": "<p>Use them to break up a firing line. They are fragile enough that any hit will likely kill one, so the threat is positioning: the detonation punishes the melee character who finishes it. Warn players once, then let the reaction do its work.</p>",
      "publication": {
        "title": "Mass Effect Compendium",
        "authors": "nscarpinatodev",
        "license": "ORC",
        "remaster": true
      },
      "languages": {
        "value": [],
        "details": ""
      },
      "blurb": "Cerberus quadruped attack drone that closes fast, bites with electrified claws, and detonates when destroyed."
